From 85e7cb0eb93de4dd83705c52e5014cae6069b785 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vittix Panchang Dev <dev@vittix.local>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 10:17:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Ascendant (Lagna) and Rahu/Ketu mean node support

- Extract SiderealTimeCalculator from SolarEventCalculator's private
  GMST implementation (behavior-preserving; sunrise/sunset outputs
  verified unchanged).
- Add Body::RahuMean / Body::KetuMean, wired into
  PurePhpAstronomyEngine::position() by exposing the omega term
  already computed internally by LunarArgumentCalculator for nutation.
- Add AscendantCalculator (Astronomy/Coordinates), implementing Meeus
  eq. 32.1 for Ascendant longitude. Depends on AstronomyEngineInterface
  rather than a standalone ayanamsha, so it stays consistent with
  whichever engine/ayanamsha the caller configures.
- Add AscendantPosition value object and $panchang->ascendant() on the
  Panchang facade.
- Add unit tests for all of the above.

These are the first two building blocks toward full Kundali support
(the remaining, larger piece is VSOP87-based positions for Mercury,
Venus, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn).
